guide forever/reputation/centaur-clans
title Gelkis and Magram Centaur Reputation
category Reputation
folder Reputation · World
levels 30-60
zone Desolace
keywords Gelkis Clan Centaur, Magram Clan Centaur, centaur, Desolace, Uthek the Wise, Warug, Captain Pentigast, Gurda Wildmane, Molkar, Gorhak, Buying Friendship, Economic Warfare, Carved Centaur Totem, Maraudine, Valley of Bones, Shen'dralas, Nerlokh, Orgrul, Khan Jehn, Ongeku, Kolkar, Centaur Banner Deployment Device, A Conqueror's Crown, Conqueror's Helm, title
why Desolace's feuding clans, reworked in Forever: pick one, buy its friendship, and trade totems for recipes.
reward item 269901
reward text 12 recipes for Carved Centaur Totems at the clan quartermasters, no standing needed
reward text Khan Jehn's quest: a clan title and a choice of three rare level 35 weapons

# Built from Forever's data: both clans start Neutral 2,000 (Forever's client faction table; Friendly is 1,000
# away, Honored 7,000, Revered 19,000, Exalted 40,000); the kill rows (a Magram kill gives the Gelkis 20 and
# costs the Magram 100, and the other way round; their khans and Warug's bodyguards 100 and 500); the quest rows
# with Forever's values (the choice quests Strange Alliance, Gelkis Alliance, Brutal Politics and Magram Alliance
# 250 and, per Forever's change log, no longer a loss with the other clan; Raid on the Kolkar, Assault on the
# Kolkar, Stealing Supplies and Broken Tears 500; Ongeku and Gizmo for Warug 1,000); Forever's new quests: Buying
# Friendship 3,000 (needs Neutral), Economic Warfare 750 for 5 Carved Centaur Totems (repeatable), the
# profession turn-ins 1,000 (Friendly), A Conqueror's Crown 1,000 (Friendly), the Valley of Bones quests 125 to
# 500 (Honored) and Khan Jehn 6,000 with a title and a choice of rare weapons (Forever's quest pages; the weapons'
# kind and stats from the client item table); the totem drops (Maraudine centaurs) and Gorhak's 12 recipes. The
# totems bind to no one (client item table): they trade and sell.
# Molkar, the Gelkis quartermaster, has no spawn in our data: he is placed from a player report from the beta.
# The Valley of Bones lies in Shen'dralas, Forever's new zone south of Desolace, which the beta (capped at level
# 30) never opened: only the quests whose giver is in the data are steps; the rest are named in the tips.
# ASSUMED: Captain Pentigast gives Buying Friendship: Magram (93226) to the Alliance as he gives the Gelkis one
# (Forever's data has no sure giver for 93226: one dialog capture names Gorhak, but the quest text sends you to
# "their quartermaster in Magram Village to the southeast", Nijel's Point's view). In-game check: who offers it?
# INGAME: Where do centaur kills stop: at the end of Friendly (Forever's kill rows) or at the end of Honored
# (Classic Era players report 11,999/12,000 Honored)?
# ASSUMED: The Magram's Valley of Bones needs A Conqueror's Crown first (Forever's quest pages list it in the
# Magram series between Broken Tears and Valley of Bones; the Gelkis series has no such step). Its Conqueror's
# Helm has no source in Forever's data; Warug sends you to "a crypt" in the Badlands. In-game check: does Warug
# offer Valley of Bones without it, and where is the helm?
# INGAME: grey-quest rep. In Classic a quest paid full only while at most 5 levels below you, then a fifth less
# per level down to a fifth (Buying Friendship, level 45, would pay 600 at 60); a Forever beta report says quests
# paid in full at any level. Economic Warfare is a level 60 quest: never cut.

step Pick your clan
  tip The Gelkis (south-west Desolace) and the Magram (south-east) are at war: every kill of one clan gives the other 20 and costs its own clan 100, so you can only climb with one. Both start Neutral. Forever's quests are worth far more than kills now, and the choice quests no longer cost the other clan anything. Alliance: Captain Pentigast at Nijel's Point offers Strange Alliance (Gelkis) and Brutal Politics (Magram). Horde: Gurda Wildmane, east of Shadowprey, offers Gelkis Alliance and Magram Alliance. Take the one of your clan and its Buying Friendship (3,000 for carrying a tote of totems), then tick the task. The guide goes on with the Gelkis; take the Magram's quests instead and it jumps to the Magram half. Do the clan's quests by level 50 if you can: in Classic a quest pays less once it is 6 or more levels below you, down to a fifth.
  accept 1382 optional only Alliance  -- Strange Alliance: Gelkis
  accept 93227 optional only Alliance -- Buying Friendship: Gelkis
  accept 1368 optional only Horde     -- Gelkis Alliance
  accept 94873 optional only Horde    -- Buying Friendship: Gelkis
  task "Take the quests of one clan"

step Gelkis Village: Uthek and Molkar
  skipto magram when onquest 1385
  skipto magram when onquest 1367
  tip Gelkis Village sits in the hills of south-west Desolace; Uthek the Wise stands at its heart. Molkar, the Gelkis quartermaster, is at the south end of the village. Buying Friendship alone takes you from Neutral to Friendly.
  turnin 1382 only Alliance           -- Uthek the Wise: 250
  accept 1384 only Alliance           -- Raid on the Kolkar
  turnin 1368 only Horde              -- Uthek the Wise: 250
  accept 1370 only Horde              -- Stealing Supplies
  turnin 93227 @35.6,92.0 only Alliance -- Molkar: 3,000
  turnin 94873 @35.6,92.0 only Horde  -- Molkar: 3,000

step Gelkis: the Kolkar camps
  only Alliance
  tip The Kolkar centaurs (level 30-33) hold the camps south of Nijel's Point, along the eastern road. About one in four drops a Crude Charm.
  collect 6079 x10 quest 1384.1 @69.5,44.0 -- Crude Charm: Kolkar centaurs
  turnin 1384                         -- Uthek the Wise: 500
  accept 1370

step Gelkis: Magram Village
  tip The Sacks of Meat lie about Magram Village, in the south-east. Every Magram you kill on the way pays the Gelkis 20.
  collect 6069 x6 quest 1370.1 @69.8,77.9 -- Crudely Dried Meat: Sacks of Meat
  kill 4640 optional                  -- Magram Wrangler: 20 Gelkis
  kill 4641 optional                  -- Magram Windchaser: 20 Gelkis

step Gelkis: Ongeku
  tip Back to Uthek, then east to the Swamp of Sorrows: Ongeku (level 37) waits by a black cauldron in Fallow Sanctuary, north-east of Stonard.
  turnin 1370                         -- Uthek the Wise: 500
  accept 1373
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  collect 6190 quest 1373.1           -- Draenethyst Shard: Ongeku
  zone Desolace
  turnin 1373                         -- Uthek the Wise: 1,000

step Gelkis: totems and kills to Honored
  tip Friendly to Honored is 6,000; after the clan's quests you are about 4,000 into it, so 2,000 to go. Molkar's Economic Warfare takes 5 Carved Centaur Totems for 750, again and again: three turn-ins, 15 totems. The Maraudine centaurs (level 36-40) of western Desolace drop them; the totems do not bind, so the auction house is the other source. Magram kills add 20 each, but Forever's kill data stops them at the end of Friendly, 1 short of Honored. At Friendly the village also has three craft orders for 1,000 each: Halea wants 3 Greater Mystic Essences, Molkar a White Bandit Mask (tailoring) and Talra a Barbaric Harness (leatherworking). Legacy Diplomat adds up to 10%.
  collect 254432 x5 optional @29.5,58.0 -- Carved Centaur Totem: Maraudine centaurs
  accept 92812 @35.6,92.0 optional    -- Economic Warfare
  turnin 92812 @35.6,92.0 optional    -- Molkar: 750
  rep 92 Honored

step Gelkis: the Valley of Bones
  tip At Honored, Uthek sends you east to Nerlokh at the southern entrance of the Valley of Bones, in Shen'dralas. Nerlokh's quests (500 each) take you among the undead and the outcasts there: Ravaging Ravagers, Outing Outcasts and Facing the Truth, then A Cleansing Cry from Uthek, and a second line (Saving Our Own, Bone Burying, Checking Things Out) that ends with Khan Jehn: kill the Magram khan in his own village for 6,000, a title and a rare level 35 weapon. They all ask you to stay Honored or better. Honored to Revered is 12,000: the valley's quests pay about 10,600 of it, two or three Economic Warfare turn-ins the rest.
  accept 93034                        -- Uthek the Wise: Valley of Bones
  zone Shen'dralas
  turnin 93034                        -- Nerlokh: 125
  accept 93035 optional
  accept 93037 optional
  accept 93041 optional
  zone Desolace

step Gelkis: Khan Jehn
  when available 93128
  tip Khan Jehn (level 37) leads the Magram from the west side of Magram Village, with his bodyguards. The kill costs the Magram 500. Uthek pays 6,000, a title, and your pick of three rare level 35 weapons: Abandoned Ferocity (two-handed axe: Strength, Stamina, Agility), Bludgeon of Betrayed Virtues (one-handed mace: Strength, Stamina, Agility) or Thrice-Damned Effigy (off-hand: Spirit, Intellect, Stamina).
  zone Shen'dralas
  accept 93128                        -- Nerlokh
  zone Desolace
  kill 5601 @66.0,80.4                -- Khan Jehn
  turnin 93128                        -- Uthek the Wise: 6,000

